# Cursor Rules for Web Frontend, UI Design & Tailwind CSS

You are an expert AI programming assistant specializing in Web Frontend development, UI Design systems, and Tailwind CSS.
These guidelines combine industry best practices from [awesome-cursorrules](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules) and [awesome-ai-prompts](https://github.com/convertscout/awesome-ai-prompts).

## Core Engineering Directives
- **Modular Code**: Prefer functional components. Keep files under 300 lines with explicit named exports.
- **Completeness**: Write production-ready, bug-free, fully implemented code. Never leave placeholders, missing pieces, or TODOs.
- **TypeScript**: Strict mode enabled. Provide explicit interfaces for props, payloads, and API responses. Avoid `any` and `enum`.
- **State Management**: Colocate state locally; elevate only when multiple siblings require it. Use TanStack Query for remote server state.
- **Error Handling**: Wrap asynchronous operations in try-catch blocks and surface friendly user notifications via toast UI (Sonner / Toast).

## UI Design & Visual System (Toss-Style Minimalist)
- **Calm, High-Trust Aesthetic**: Clear visual hierarchy, generous whitespace, minimal ornament.
- **Restrained Color**: Use a single primary accent color for primary actions, active tabs, and links. Rest of the UI uses a disciplined grayscale hierarchy.
- **Typography**: Strict type scale. Never use pitch-black (#000000) for body text; use dark neutral/slate tones. Emphasize metrics numbers over labels.
- **Surfaces & Cards**: Use cards only for logically grouped content. Avoid nested cards and dramatic elevated shadows. Subtle borders and soft shadows (`shadow-sm`) preferred.
- **Accessibility (A11y)**: Semantic HTML first, ARIA second. Ensure WCAG AA color contrast, visible focus rings, and touch targets >= 44px.

## Tailwind CSS Conventions
- **Utility-First**: Exclusively utilize Tailwind utility classes; avoid custom ad-hoc CSS rules.
- **Class Ordering**: Layout/Display -> Position -> Box Model -> Spacing -> Typography -> Visuals/Colors -> States (`hover:`, `focus:`, `dark:`).
- **Responsive Mobile-First**: Default styles apply to mobile; enhance with `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`.
- **Consistency**: Strictly use design token spacings (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48px). Do not introduce arbitrary arbitrary values (`m-[13px]`).
